  {"heading":"New factory / Nouvelle \"factory\"","segment_index":"S4.P3","kind":"untrue","en_span":"chapters/reportfactory.qmd:52-52","tr_span":"chapters/reportfactory.fr.qmd:51-51","proposition":"The English says the R scripts in the \"scripts\" folder are sourced BY the Rmd scripts (the Rmd calls them); the French says those scripts \"proviennent de vos scripts Rmd\" (come from / originate in your Rmd scripts), which reverses the direction of the relationship.","reader_consequence":"A French reader understands the \"scripts\" folder as a place for code extracted out of Rmd files, rather than as a place for helper .R files that the Rmd sources at run time, so they will not set up the source() workflow the chapter is describing.","confidence":"medium"},
  {"heading":"Scripts","segment_index":"S16.P1","kind":"untrue","en_span":"chapters/reportfactory.qmd:256-256","tr_span":"chapters/reportfactory.fr.qmd:253-253","proposition":"The English says the \"scripts\" folder stores runfiles or .R scripts that are sourced BY your .Rmd scripts; the French says \"les scripts .R qui proviennent de vos scripts .Rmd\" (the .R scripts that come from your .Rmd scripts), reversing which file calls which.","reader_consequence":"The reader misses the recommended structure of splitting code across files where the Rmd sources helper .R scripts, and instead reads the folder as an archive of code taken out of Rmd files.","confidence":"medium"}
